title: $:/mf/gen/CLI command/mf slow
catalog: CLI command
target: mf slow
summary: Slow-operation log: what took seconds, and where the time went

!! Reference

```
Slow-operation log: what took seconds, and where the time went

Usage: mf slow [OPTIONS]
       mf slow <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list    List the slow operations, newest first — the default
  replay  Run a query again and show where its time goes, now: the newest logged query, the one logged at --at, or one typed with -q. Not itself logged
  clear   Empty the log (the clean slate a reproduction starts from)
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --limit <LIMIT>
          How many entries to show (newest first)
          
          [default: 50]

  -d, --since <SINCE>
          Only entries from the last duration (e.g. 30m, 12h, 7d)

      --op <OP>
          Only entries whose operation contains this substring

      --min <MIN>
          Only entries that took at least this long (e.g. 30s, 2m, 1h)

      --json
          Print the raw entries, one JSON object per line

  -h, --help
          Print help
```
